{"format_version":2,"scenario":{"format_version":2,"name":"Process crash · uncommitted transaction","description":"A changes a row inside an open transaction, then its worker process is forcibly terminated between statements. A new worker opens the same database file. Queries, not journal files, establish the outcome: the original rows remain, the old transaction is gone and new writes succeed. This models the abrupt end of one process, not power loss. https://www.sqlite.org/atomiccommit.html","settings":{"journal_mode":"wal","busy_ms":2000,"deadline_ms":5000,"row_limit":100,"connections":2},"initial":["CREATE TABLE account(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, balance INTEGER NOT NULL)","INSERT INTO account VALUES (1, 100), (2, 50)"],"operations":[{"id":"a_begin","connection":"A","sql":"BEGIN IMMEDIATE","params":[],"after":[],"expect":null,"note":"A starts a write transaction."},{"id":"a_update","connection":"A","sql":"UPDATE account SET balance = balance - 30 WHERE id = 1","params":[],"after":[{"operation":"a_begin","event":"completed"}],"expect":null,"note":"Change a row without committing."},{"id":"a_own_view","connection":"A","sql":"SELECT id, balance FROM account ORDER BY id","params":[],"after":[{"operation":"a_update","event":"completed"}],"expect":{"rows":[[{"type":"integer","value":"1"},{"type":"integer","value":"70"}],[{"type":"integer","value":"2"},{"type":"integer","value":"50"}]]},"note":"Inside its transaction A reads its own uncommitted change."},{"id":"a_crash","connection":"A","kind":"crash","sql":"","params":[],"after":[{"operation":"a_own_view","event":"completed"}],"expect":null,"note":"Forcibly terminate A's worker process after the confirmed statement. No ROLLBACK or close runs."},{"id":"b_while_closed","connection":"B","sql":"SELECT id, balance FROM account ORDER BY id","params":[],"after":[{"operation":"a_crash","event":"completed"}],"expect":{"rows":[[{"type":"integer","value":"1"},{"type":"integer","value":"100"}],[{"type":"integer","value":"2"},{"type"